*.bin binary

# The turn-verdict prompt is the ONE source read by two programs on two platforms - the product
# embeds it and the grading tool in the internal repository reads it off disk. A checkout that
# rewrote its line endings would make the embedded copy and the file on disk differ by every line,
# and the test that pins them together would pass on one machine and fail on the next. Pin it.
src/CcDirector.Core/Wingman/Prompts/*.txt text eol=lf

# Pi wire logs are byte-exact recordings: the framing tests read the line feeds Pi wrote. A checkout
# that turned them into carriage return plus line feed would test a stream Pi never sends.
src/CcDirector.Core.Tests/TestData/pi-rpc/*.jsonl -text
docs/missions/api-mode-pi-2026-10-16/preamble-proof/*.jsonl -text

# The built-in Mail Desk factory template is hashed into its template version, which decides whether an account is
# offered a new draft. A checkout that rewrote its line endings would give one template two versions, one per build
# machine. Pin it.
src/CcDirector.Gateway/MailDesk/Template/** text eol=lf

# The Mail Desk prompts are sent to the model byte for byte, and the tests pin the exact request. A checkout that
# rewrote their line endings would send a Windows-built Gateway's model different text from a Linux-built one's, and
# the tests would pass on one machine and fail on the next. The phase 0 copies the prompts were measured with are
# pinned with them, because a test holds the two equal byte for byte.
src/CcDirector.Gateway/MailDesk/Prompts/*.txt text eol=lf
docs/qa/mail-desk/phase-0/c-model/prompts/*.txt text eol=lf
